      en: "The Ildo Lobo Palace of Culture in Mindelo, named after the iconic morna singer, opened in 2004 as a hub for performing arts. The contemporary building features a 500-seat auditorium, exhibition halls, rehearsal spaces, and a media library. It hosts the annual Morna Festival and other cultural events. In 2012, an outdoor amphitheater was added, increasing capacity for open-air concerts. Funded by the European Union, the palace cost €2 million. It has become a landmark for Cape Verdean music and arts, preserving the legacy of Ildo Lobo and promoting contemporary creativity.",
